  "outcome": "pending_approval",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Tom, I found the problem. Harborview Supplies' email \"Invoice #4471 - October pallets\" did arrive this morning, but our spam filter held it back. I've asked for it to be released to your inbox. A technician needs to approve that first, and once they do it should show up in your inbox. Could you let us know when you see it? Also, your account is currently locked after several wrong password attempts this morning. If you're having trouble signing in, reply here or call the help desk and we'll help you get back in.",
  "internal_note": "KB-007: The quarantine for tom.becker has Q-1004 from billing@harborview-supplies.example, subject \"Invoice #4471 - October pallets\", received 2026-10-09 12:26 UTC. It was held as spam and is releasable. It matches the vendor and invoice number the user gave, and I didn't see a look-alike domain. I queued release_email for Q-1004 (approval id 1). Do NOT release Q-1005 (scanner@docs-share.example, \"Scanned document 0931.zip\"): it is marked malware and is not releasable. The user didn't ask about it. Something else I noticed: the account status is locked after 5 failed_password attempts on 2026-10-09 between 09:46 and 10:01 ET. They all came from the corporate IP 203.0.113.10 in New York during his usual hours, and his history shows normal Duo-approved sign-ins. It looks like he mistyped his password, not a compromise. He didn't ask for an unlock, so I didn't queue one. If he asks, unlock per standard process after confirming it's him.",
